# {{name}}

Lazuli `{{namespace}}` adapter plugin. Binds a Go interface and declares an
environment-variable contract. Scaffolded with `lazuli plugin new --kind adapter`.

## Status

- Go server adapter — `Adapter` satisfies the `Interface` it `implements`,
  auto-registers via `init()` against `{{namespace}}`.

## Usage

In `Lazurite.toml`:

```toml
[plugins]
"{{namespace}}" = { module = "{{module}}", version = "v0.1.0" }
```

Declare the required env vars in `manifest.toml [env]` and read them in
`newAdapter()`.

## Wire it up

1. Replace the placeholder `Interface` in `adapter.go` with the real
   `lazuli.dev/runtime/lazuli/<domain>.<Interface>` you implement.
2. Uncomment the `lazuli.RegisterAdapter(AdapterRef, newAdapter())` line in
   `init()` once you import the runtime.
3. Fill the method stubs (currently returning `ErrUnimplemented`) with real
   upstream-SDK calls. Stay wire-thin — no business logic in the adapter.

